  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Strengthening the capacity of at least 335,000 people living along river banks in the Chadian Sahelian Belt to better withstand flooding and drought</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This activity Strengthening the capacity of at least 335,000 people living along river banks in the Chadian Sahelian Belt to better withstand flooding and drought is a component of Building Resilience and Adaptation to Climate Extremes and Disasters reported by FCDO with a funding type of 111 - Not for profit organisation and a budget of &#xa3;169,963. This project benefits South of Sahara, regional. It works in the following sector(s): Environmental policy and administrative management.</narrative>
  </description>
